WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:01.920
- Did your parents, were they encouraging

00:00:01.920 --> 00:00:02.920
with you singing or were they,

00:00:02.920 --> 00:00:05.030
cause my mom was an
educator so she was kind of

00:00:05.030 --> 00:00:07.890
slightly like, "Hmm, I
think you should maybe

00:00:07.890 --> 00:00:09.550
still go to college." Like, were your

00:00:09.550 --> 00:00:12.862
parents encouraging?
- Yes. (laughs)

00:00:12.862 --> 00:00:14.060
I think, I mean they were
definitely encouraging

00:00:14.060 --> 00:00:17.470
but I think my dad
especially was a little bit

00:00:17.470 --> 00:00:19.250
more skeptical of the, you know,

00:00:19.250 --> 00:00:21.580
this whole thing as a
career, I think because

00:00:21.580 --> 00:00:24.240
my whole family was like
so far removed from like,

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:25.380
anything to do with the industry.

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:26.380
Like they didn't know what it was,

00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:28.180
they didn't think it
was, like, a real thing

00:00:28.180 --> 00:00:29.270
that you could do with your life.

00:00:29.270 --> 00:00:31.970
And, I mean, realistically
it doesn't happen to everyone

00:00:31.970 --> 00:00:33.430
so I did get really lucky but,

00:00:33.430 --> 00:00:35.370
yeah they were definitely,
you know, try to

00:00:35.370 --> 00:00:38.370
persuade me to, like, go to
college and do the whole, like,

00:00:38.370 --> 00:00:40.060
take the educational route, but,

00:00:40.060 --> 00:00:42.369
thankfully this happened
before I could do that so,

00:00:42.369 --> 00:00:43.520
(laughs) it worked out.

00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:45.540
- That's awesome, (laughs) that's amazing.

00:00:45.540 --> 00:00:48.420
So what kind of music
did your parents like

00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:49.253
when you were young?

00:00:49.253 --> 00:00:51.470
Like, cause your sound
is really rad and I was

00:00:51.470 --> 00:00:52.810
think it's interesting to know people's,

00:00:52.810 --> 00:00:54.520
I was the youngest in my family so I had

00:00:54.520 --> 00:00:56.650
all these different
influences coming at me,

00:00:56.650 --> 00:00:58.810
so what were your
parents, like, what music

00:00:58.810 --> 00:01:00.740
did you grow up around?

00:01:00.740 --> 00:01:02.870
- Well my mom listened to
a lot of Italian music.

00:01:02.870 --> 00:01:05.370
We're Italian, so she, you
know, was born and raised there,

00:01:05.370 --> 00:01:08.070
so she played a lot of Italian music.

00:01:08.070 --> 00:01:10.650
And then my dad played a lot
of, like, traditional, like,

00:01:10.650 --> 00:01:12.840
you know Beatles and
Queen and I'm not even

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:15.200
just saying this, because it's you,

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:18.630
right now, but he loved your album.

00:01:18.630 --> 00:01:20.355
Like, we, I grew up on you.

00:01:20.355 --> 00:01:22.160
- Oh, that's awesome.
- Just because, like my dad,

00:01:22.160 --> 00:01:23.650
like, we went on this
road trip, we were like

00:01:23.650 --> 00:01:25.760
driving to Florida and
that's the only thing

00:01:25.760 --> 00:01:27.530
he played for the entirety of the two days

00:01:27.530 --> 00:01:28.574
that we were driving and I--

00:01:28.574 --> 00:01:30.107
- Okay he is amazing.
- I loved it.

00:01:30.107 --> 00:01:31.970
(Kelly laughs)
No, I loved it,

00:01:31.970 --> 00:01:32.980
I mean I love your music, I would've

00:01:32.980 --> 00:01:35.640
listened to it anyways but
like my dad was obsessed

00:01:35.640 --> 00:01:38.113
with your first album.
- I love how random that is.

00:01:38.113 --> 00:01:40.020
That's amazing.
- I know, I swear to god,

00:01:40.020 --> 00:01:41.030
like I'm not even just saying that.

00:01:41.030 --> 00:01:43.060
I know your entire first
album off by heart,

00:01:43.060 --> 00:01:44.267
cause of my dad, so,

00:01:44.267 --> 00:01:45.260
there you go.
- Well what's funny though is

00:01:45.260 --> 00:01:47.540
you mentioned your mother
loved Italian music.

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:49.700
That's cool that your
mom was listening to that

00:01:49.700 --> 00:01:51.310
when you had that in your
ear, like growing up.

00:01:51.310 --> 00:01:52.770
Not every kid gets that.

